note Source: Go bufio/scan.go, (*Scanner).setErr.

note GAP: errors as stored values - Go keeps the first error in a field of type error, and
note io.EOF is one particular value of that open interface type. Scribe failures are names in
note `fails with` lines, not values that can be stored or compared. A closed choice stands in
note for the open error interface, so errors from any io.Reader cannot be added later.
choice ScanError
    EndOfFile
    TooLong
    NegativeAdvance
    AdvanceTooFar
    BadReadCount
    FinalToken
    ReaderError with reason as Text

type Scanner
    field err as a maybe ScanError

note setErr records the first non-EOF error.
note WORKAROUND: Go's receiver (s *Scanner) becomes an editable parameter; there are no methods.
to set_err err on scanner
    given err is a ScanError
    given scanner is an editable Scanner

    note WORKAROUND: Go tests `s.err == nil || s.err == io.EOF` in one condition. A maybe value
    note can only be opened with `choose`, so the two cases become two `when` branches.
    choose err of scanner
        when nothing
            set err of scanner to some err
        when some current
            if current is EndOfFile
                set err of scanner to some err
